        <li><p><strong>Turn your ballot over.</strong> Question 2 is on the back; the front says “VOTE BOTH SIDES.” <Cite id="farmington-sample-ballot" /></p></li>
        <li><p><strong>Don’t skip it.</strong> District leaders have said a blank isn’t counted in the 60%, but the law doesn’t say so directly, and under another reading a blank would in effect count as a No. As of Oct. 21 I hadn’t found guidance from the Attorney General’s office. Mark the choice you mean. <Cite id="school-board-video" href={vid(2372)} label="Video, 39:32" /> <Cite id="nhpr-cuts" /> <a href="#unknowns">Why it’s unsettled</a></p></li>
